Professional Definition
Definition

An encounter is an interaction between a patient and a healthcare provider or healthcare organization for the purpose of providing or managing healthcare services.

An encounter can represent different types of healthcare interactions, such as an outpatient visit, emergency department visit, inpatient stay, or other clinical interaction, depending on how the healthcare system defines and records it.

In an EHR, an encounter generally provides context for clinical information such as diagnoses, procedures, observations, medications, orders, and notes.

An encounter is not necessarily the same thing as a claim. One encounter may generate one or more claims, and some encounters may not result in a claim.

Category

Healthcare / Clinical Data / EHR

Why it matters

For a health data analyst, the encounter is often an important way to organize and analyze clinical activity.

For example, encounter data can be used to calculate:

Number of outpatient visits
Emergency department utilization
Inpatient admissions
Length of stay
Provider utilization
Diagnosis and procedure patterns
Readmission metrics
Patient visit frequency

An analyst needs to understand what the organization's definition of an encounter is before using it in a metric.

Simple example

A patient visits a primary care clinic for a follow-up appointment.

The EHR may create an encounter with information such as:

Encounter ID: ENC10025
Patient ID: P1001
Encounter Type: Outpatient
Date: 2026-08-10
Provider ID: PR204
Location: Primary Care
Status: Completed

The diagnoses, vital signs, laboratory orders, medications, and clinical notes associated with that visit can be connected to the encounter.

Important distinction

An encounter describes a healthcare interaction.

A claim describes a request for payment/reimbursement.

They can be related, but they are not the same concept.

Review note: Encounter definitions and encounter types can vary by EHR, organization, implementation, and healthcare workflow. Verify the specific definition used by the source system before building a metric.
